# No trailing slashes on the directory names. A pattern ending in "/" matches
# directories only, so it silently misses a symlink of the same name - and in a
# git worktree the heavy shared artifacts are exactly what gets symlinked back to
# the main checkout. Both vendor and node_modules showed up as untracked that way.
node_modules
dist
vendor
native/build
captures
.playwright-cli
*.log
.DS_Store
exports
projects
presets
.library-check
# The staged tree monitor-check builds and deletes. It only survives a run that
# threw, which is exactly when it is worth looking at and never worth committing.
.monitor-check

# Render-queue records. The queue is state a machine accumulates, not source.
jobs
.jobs-check

# One log per mutation from the full sweep, plus its SUMMARY. Minutes of machine
# output describing a tree, which the commit message carries the conclusion of.
.sweep-all

# Claude Code's per-project settings and local state. It is empty today, which is the
# only reason nobody has committed it - the moment the editor writes
# settings.local.json into it, a `git add -A` takes one machine's paths and
# permissions along for the ride.
.claude
